{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And if it be eaten at all, etc.</b> Scripture speaks of one who, at the slaughter, intends to eat it on the third day. One might think that if he ate of it on the third day it is disqualified retroactively — Scripture says, ״the one who offers it, it shall not be imputed״: it is disqualified at the time of offering, and is not disqualified on the third day. And so its meaning: at the time of its offering, this does not enter his mind, and if he did intend it, it becomes פִּגּוּל (Zevaḥim 29)." "<b>And the soul that eats of it.</b> Even within the time limit — <b>shall bear his iniquity.</b>"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:22.849552170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}